the element shapes are UniProt's, as they occur in the UniProt 2026_03 human gene-centric XML.

What it exercises:
 - Q9ZZZ1 displays isoform Q9ZZZ1-2, not -1 (UniProt's displayed isoform can carry any number);
 - an interaction comment whose <interactant><id> must not be read as an isoform id;
 - isoform <sequence type="described"> elements, which must not replace the entry's own <sequence>;
 - a text-form <molecule> inside a comment, which is not a dbReference's molecule;
 - dbReferences scoped to one isoform by <molecule id>: Ensembl, and Reactome for the displayed and a non-displayed
   isoform, interleaved with whole-entry references so a molecule cannot leak into the next reference;
 - Q9ZZZ2 lists no isoforms.
-->
